hw encoder: zero-copy DMA-BUF input to the bcm2835 codec

Import the libcamera frame's DMA-BUF straight into the codec OUTPUT queue
(V4L2_MEMORY_DMABUF) instead of CPU-copying the YUV frame. On the Pi the ISP
dmabuf is uncached to the ARM, so the old per-row memcpy cost ~200-400 ms/frame
(CP_IN); DMA-BUF import makes it ~0. CAPTURE (MJPEG out) stays MMAP.

Signed-off-by: webcampi <webcampi@localhost>

